WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.175
Hi, I'm Domino!

00:00:02.175 --> 00:00:05.421
The whole nervous system of a male fruit fly has been

00:00:05.421 --> 00:00:06.601
mapped, neuron by neuron.

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:09.552
Here's what that map is, and what it can compute.

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:14.278
The idea: that map is a substrate, not a model.

00:00:14.278 --> 00:00:18.842
Weights, timing and neuromodulation are not in it; every model supplies them itself.

00:00:20.483 --> 00:00:25.189
Electron microscopy images the brain slice by slice, at nanometer resolution.

00:00:25.609 --> 00:00:30.463
Software traces each neuron through thousands of sections, and people proofread the result.

00:00:30.883 --> 00:00:35.607
It finds every synapse, and a classifier guesses which transmitter each one releases.

00:00:36.027 --> 00:00:39.277
The output is a graph: who connects to whom, and how many

00:00:39.277 --> 00:00:40.361
contacts back each link.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:47.476
One: copy the visual wiring exactly, and train only what anatomy leaves open.

00:00:47.476 --> 00:00:51.650
Seven hundred and thirty-four parameters for over forty-five thousand neurons.

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:55.544
It predicted the tuning of real, named cells it never saw.

00:00:55.544 --> 00:00:58.070
A random network the same size did worse.

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:01.662
Two: freeze everything and train only a linear readout.

00:01:01.662 --> 00:01:04.834
Scramble the wiring, keep its statistics, and it ties.

00:01:05.254 --> 00:01:09.058
Three: put it in a simulated body, and ask what real mass

00:01:09.058 --> 00:01:11.277
and contact forces demand of any controller.

00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:17.895
In an escape circuit, real wiring reached ninety percent in about thirty

00:01:17.895 --> 00:01:19.984
iterations; shuffled wiring took seventy-seven.

00:01:19.984 --> 00:01:24.161
Same final accuracy: a better starting point, not a requirement.

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:29.050
So the connectome matters exactly when you care about which neuron,

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:30.243
not just how many.

00:01:32.775 --> 00:01:35.835
To recap: a map of contacts, not a model.

00:01:35.835 --> 00:01:38.895
Readouts see its statistics; named cells need its identity.

00:01:39.315 --> 00:01:41.450
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:42.060
I'm Domino.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:42.365
Bye!
